      "mergeID": "6a30a0279087ecf78a360e9d",
      "mergedPostDetails": "I updated my word description over the webpage and added a link to a Discord server. After saving, the slash in the url turns to a weird symbol (looks a sort of a slash, but it isn't). Copy & pasting the url doesn't work because of a invalid char.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "'Slash' in a world description turns to an invalid symbol",
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "690cca0cf7f938ffc3fcf403",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "When will this be fixed? With the enhancement of group functionality, there is a growing demand for sharing URLs, but it hasn't been fixed. I looked into it and found that it has been left untouched for two years, since 2023. Is there no decent web engineer on the VRChat development team?",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
